			<item>
				<title>Cova de Cala Falcó</title>
				<link>/posts/cova-de-cala-falc%C3%B3/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>/posts/cova-de-cala-falc%C3%B3/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;details&#34;&gt;Details&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;identification&#34;&gt;Identification&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feature type:&lt;/strong&gt; Cave&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; Mindat.org&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;cave-and-exploration-data&#34;&gt;Cave and exploration data&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cave rating:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exploration potential:&lt;/strong&gt; Medium&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tourism potential:&lt;/strong&gt; Medium&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disabled access potential:&lt;/strong&gt; Low&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Goes to water:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;references&#34;&gt;References&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mindat.org:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.mindat.org/loc-290943.html&#34;&gt;https://www.mindat.org/loc-290943.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wikipedia:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cala_Falc%C3%B3&#34;&gt;https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cala_Falc%C3%B3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(Translated from German) &amp;ldquo;In the immediate vicinity of Cala Falcó there are several cave systems that are partially accessible and have underground lakes. These include, to the west and north of the bay, the &lt;a href=&#34;/posts/cova-de-sa-piqueta/&#34;&gt;Cova de sa Piqueta&lt;/a&gt; , the Cova des Pont , the &lt;a href=&#34;/posts/cova-des-xots/&#34;&gt;Cova des Xots&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href=&#34;/posts/cova-des-pirata/&#34;&gt;Cova des Pirata&lt;/a&gt; . On the coast to the northeast are the Cova des Moroand southeast the &lt;a href=&#34;/posts/cova-des-coloms/&#34;&gt;Cova des Coloms&lt;/a&gt;, accessible only by water . Directly on the north side of the bay is the entrance to the Cova de Cala Falcó , a karst cave that is no longer illuminated a few meters behind the entrance.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
