				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;about&#34;&gt;About&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;+1km of tunnel. Site where two divers had the line break and one of them had to wait 2.5 days to be rescued from an air chamber&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;details&#34;&gt;Details&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;identification&#34;&gt;Identification&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feature type:&lt;/strong&gt; Cave&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System name:&lt;/strong&gt; Pirata-Pont-Piqueta&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; MapCarta&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;cave-and-exploration-data&#34;&gt;Cave and exploration data&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cave rating:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vertical access:&lt;/strong&gt; No&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exploration potential:&lt;/strong&gt; Medium&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tourism potential:&lt;/strong&gt; Medium&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Goes to water:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;additional-notes&#34;&gt;Additional Notes&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wikipedia:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cova_des_Pont&#34;&gt;https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cova_des_Pont&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(Translated from German) &amp;ldquo;The entrance to the Cova des Pont is located 480 meters from the east coast of Mallorca at Cala Falcó within the Cales Verges de Manacor nature reserve . The next town, S&amp;rsquo;Estany d&amp;rsquo;en Mas, is 1080 meters to the north, the bay of Cala Varques 830 meters to the south and the historic fortified tower of Son Fortesa 1840 meters to the west.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
