			<item>
				<title>Cova de sa Campana</title>
				<link>/posts/cova-de-sa-campana/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>/posts/cova-de-sa-campana/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;details&#34;&gt;Details&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;identification&#34;&gt;Identification&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feature type:&lt;/strong&gt; Cave&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; Mapcarta&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;additional-notes&#34;&gt;Additional Notes&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;mondoaventura.com:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://mondaventura.com/es/actividades-aventura-mallorca-pollensa/tours-excursiones-guiadas/espeleologia-cuevas/cueva-terrestre-cova-sa-campana/&#34;&gt;https://mondaventura.com/es/actividades-aventura-mallorca-pollensa/tours-excursiones-guiadas/espeleologia-cuevas/cueva-terrestre-cova-sa-campana/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;The Sa Campana cave , of great biological and speleological interest, is the second deepest cave (up to -350 meters!) and one of the most beautiful in Mallorca. We can divide it into several sectors of different difficulty, made up of huge rooms and a multitude of formations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our route will take us through impressive rooms, full of formations of all kinds: lava flows, cat flaps, gours, wells&amp;hellip; all of them spectacular due to their sizes and shapes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
